## Course overview

German B is a language-acquisition course for students with previous experience of German. It develops the ability to communicate clearly and appropriately across a range of contexts, audiences, and purposes, while exploring German-speaking cultures through authentic texts.

## What you will study

The course is built around five prescribed themes:

- **Identities**
- **Experiences**
- **Human ingenuity**
- **Social organisation**
- **Sharing the planet**

At HL, students also study **two literary works** in German.

## Assessment

| Component | SL | HL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (productive writing) | 25% | 25% | One written task from a choice of text types |
| Paper 2 (listening & reading) | 50% | 50% | Receptive skills assessment |
| Individual Oral | 25% | 25% | Conversation based on a visual stimulus (SL) or literary extract (HL) |
